{"source":"wine.com/activity/mywine","capturedAt":"2026-08-27","total":54,"rated":23,"wines":[{"id":"2523984","sku":"SXWGAS00223_2023","name":"Domaine Fabrice Gasnier Chinon Les Graves 2023","vintage":2023,"varietal":"Cabernet Franc","origin":"Chinon, Touraine, Loire, France","country":"France","region":"Chinon","myRating":4.5,"ratedDate":"8/2/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":3.6,"communityCount":10,"critics":[{"score":90,"source":"RobertParker"}],"priceUsd":21.97,"attrs":[],"sommName":"Josefina","sommWriteup":"We venture into a subregion of Loire called Chinon, where Cab Franc is not only the primary red varietal, but also crafted into a vibrant, acid-driven and easy-drinking wine.","path":"/product/domaine-fabrice-gasnier-chinon-les-graves-2023/2523984"},{"id":"2790484","sku":"TON83475_22_2022","name":"Petra Zingari Toscana 2022","vintage":2022,"varietal":"Tuscan Blends","origin":"Tuscany, Italy","country":"Italy","region":"Tuscany","myRating":null,"ratedDate":null,"pickedForYou":"8/2/26","communityAvg":4.4,"communityCount":54,"critics":[{"score":91,"source":"JamesSuckling"},{"score":90,"source":"WineEnthusiast"},{"score":90,"source":"WilfredWong"}],"priceUsd":17.97,"attrs":[],"sommName":"Josefina","sommWriteup":"An approachable blend of Sangiovese, Merlot, Syrah & Petit Verdot, offering black cherry, plum & a hint of Mediterranean herbs. A versatile bottle for your dinner table, that pairs beautifully with roasted veggies. Aged cheeses, like Parmigiano.","path":"/product/petra-zingari-toscana-2022/2790484"},{"id":"2283884","sku":"PIN622933_2023","name":"Schug Sonoma Coast Pinot Noir 2023","vintage":2023,"varietal":"Pinot Noir","origin":"Sonoma Coast, Sonoma County, California","country":"California","region":"Sonoma Coast","myRating":null,"ratedDate":null,"pickedForYou":"8/2/26","communityAvg":3.5,"communityCount":96,"critics":[{"score":91,"source":"JamesSuckling"},{"score":91,"source":"TastingPanel"}],"priceUsd":null,"attrs":["Screw Cap"],"sommName":"Josefina","sommWriteup":"Sourced from Carneros and the Petaluma Gap, where the fog enters and cools the area. As a result, Pinot Noir grapes mature slowly while retaining their natural acidity. Aged in neutral oak, it enhances the flavors of cherries, strawberries and spice.","path":"/product/schug-sonoma-coast-pinot-noir-2023/2283884"},{"id":"3379668","sku":"ONYSBBBAR75_21_2021","name":"Senorio de Barahonda Barrica Monastrell-Syrah 2021","vintage":2021,"varietal":"Other Red Blends","origin":"Yecla, Spain","country":"Spain","region":"Yecla","myRating":null,"ratedDate":null,"pickedForYou":"8/2/26","communityAvg":null,"communityCount":null,"critics":[{"score":90,"source":"JamesSuckling"}],"priceUsd":24.99,"attrs":[],"sommName":null,"sommWriteup":null,"path":"/product/senorio-de-barahonda-barrica-monastrell-syrah-2021/3379668"},{"id":"3478539","sku":"REG212871724_2024","name":"Domaine D'Ansignan Les Grenadines 2024","vintage":2024,"varietal":"Other Red Blends","origin":"Roussillon, South of France, France","country":"France","region":"Roussillon","myRating":null,"ratedDate":null,"pickedForYou":"8/2/26","communityAvg":null,"communityCount":null,"critics":[{"score":91,"source":"WineEnthusiast"}],"priceUsd":null,"attrs":["Green"],"sommName":null,"sommWriteup":null,"path":"/product/domaine-dansignan-les-grenadines-2024/3478539"},{"id":"3780847","sku":"ELY3780847_2022","name":"Chateau Vieux Landat 2022","vintage":2022,"varietal":"Bordeaux Red Blends","origin":"Haut Medoc, Bordeaux, France","country":"France","region":"Haut Medoc","myRating":null,"ratedDate":null,"pickedForYou":"8/2/26","communityAvg":3.6,"communityCount":15,"critics":[{"score":92,"source":"WineEnthusiast"}],"priceUsd":null,"attrs":[],"sommName":"Josefina","sommWriteup":"A Haut-Medoc estate known for Cabernet-driven balance, this vintage shows clean fruit and gentle tannins shaped by gravel soils. A straightforward, well-made Left Bank wine with an easy, modern edge.","path":"/product/chateau-vieux-landat-2022/3780847"},{"id":"3902977","sku":"SKRITVAL0122_2022","name":"Vallana Campi Raudii 2022","vintage":2022,"varietal":"Nebbiolo","origin":"Piedmont, Italy","country":"Italy","region":"Piedmont","myRating":null,"ratedDate":null,"pickedForYou":"8/2/26","communityAvg":null,"communityCount":null,"critics":[{"score":92,"source":"Vinous"},{"score":89,"source":"WineSpectator"}],"priceUsd":null,"attrs":[],"sommName":null,"sommWriteup":null,"path":"/product/vallana-campi-raudii-2022/3902977"},{"id":"1955159","sku":"WBO30318251_2022","name":"Paxton Vineyards AAA Shiraz-Grenache-Mourvedre 2022","vintage":2022,"varietal":"Rhone Blends","origin":"McLaren Vale, South Australia, Australia","country":"Australia","region":"McLaren Vale","myRating":3,"ratedDate":"7/27/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":3.7,"communityCount":11,"critics":[],"priceUsd":19.97,"attrs":["Green Screw Cap"],"sommName":null,"sommWriteup":null,"path":"/product/paxton-vineyards-aaa-shiraz-grenache-mourvedre-2022/1955159"},{"id":"2945931","sku":"DBWDB6107_23_2023","name":"Chateau Mourgues du Gres Costieres de Nimes Galets Rouge 2023","vintage":2023,"varietal":"Rhone Blends","origin":"Costieres de Nimes, Rhone, France","country":"France","region":"Costieres de Nimes","myRating":4.5,"ratedDate":"7/24/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":null,"communityCount":null,"critics":[{"score":91,"source":"JamesSuckling"}],"priceUsd":19.97,"attrs":["Green"],"sommName":null,"sommWriteup":null,"path":"/product/chateau-mourgues-du-gres-costieres-de-nimes-galets-rouge-2023/2945931"},{"id":"1097895","sku":"PIN551945_2020","name":"Leyda Las Brisas Pinot Noir 2020","vintage":2020,"varietal":"Pinot Noir","origin":"Leyda Valley, San Antonio Valley (Chile), Chile","country":"Chile","region":"Leyda Valley","myRating":4,"ratedDate":"7/20/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":2.7,"communityCount":6,"critics":[{"score":92,"source":"Vinous"}],"priceUsd":null,"attrs":["Green Screw Cap"],"sommName":null,"sommWriteup":null,"path":"/product/leyda-las-brisas-pinot-noir-2020/1097895"},{"id":"3432738","sku":"CGM64933_2022","name":"Tornatore Etna Rosso 2022","vintage":2022,"varietal":"Nerello Mascalese","origin":"Sicily, Italy","country":"Italy","region":"Sicily","myRating":4.5,"ratedDate":"7/18/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":3.6,"communityCount":34,"critics":[{"score":92,"source":"JamesSuckling"},{"score":90,"source":"JebDunnuck"},{"score":90,"source":"Vinous"}],"priceUsd":null,"attrs":[],"sommName":"Josefina","sommWriteup":"This is probably my favorite wine to drink with pizza. Grapes are destemmed and fermented in concrete, while the aging is on large wooden crates. This way the wine shows the purity of the grape: red fruits, violets with silky light tannins.","path":"/product/tornatore-etna-rosso-2022/3432738"},{"id":"4122645","sku":"TON14511_22_2022","name":"Domaine Gilles Coperet Fleurie La Madone 2022","vintage":2022,"varietal":"Gamay","origin":"Beaujolais, Burgundy, France","country":"France","region":"Beaujolais","myRating":4,"ratedDate":"7/15/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":4.8,"communityCount":27,"critics":[{"score":93,"source":"WineEnthusiast"},{"score":92,"source":"JamesSuckling"},{"score":92,"source":"WilfredWong"}],"priceUsd":null,"attrs":[],"sommName":null,"sommWriteup":null,"path":"/product/domaine-gilles-coperet-fleurie-la-madone-2022/4122645"},{"id":"4010912","sku":"TON82014_22_2022","name":"Patrizi Barbaresco 2022","vintage":2022,"varietal":"Nebbiolo","origin":"Barbaresco, Piedmont, Italy","country":"Italy","region":"Barbaresco","myRating":4,"ratedDate":"7/15/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":4.6,"communityCount":33,"critics":[{"score":91,"source":"WilfredWong"}],"priceUsd":25.97,"attrs":["Green"],"sommName":"Josefina","sommWriteup":"Barbaresco has more fertile soils and lower altitude than Barolo, in these conditions the Nebbiolo grapes develop thinner skins and moderate acidity. The resulting wines are less tannic and accessible young, with a bright red fruit flavor profile.","path":"/product/patrizi-barbaresco-2022/4010912"},{"id":"4056257","sku":"TON14540_23_2023","name":"Domaine Gaget Cote du Py Morgon 2023","vintage":2023,"varietal":"Gamay","origin":"Beaujolais, Burgundy, France","country":"France","region":"Beaujolais","myRating":3.5,"ratedDate":"7/15/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":4.3,"communityCount":54,"critics":[{"score":94,"source":"WineEnthusiast"},{"score":93,"source":"JamesSuckling"},{"score":93,"source":"WilfredWong"}],"priceUsd":null,"attrs":["Boutique Green"],"sommName":"Josefina","sommWriteup":"Morgon is the Beaujolais cru known to produce fleshy, fuller bodied expressions of Gamay with a balanced structure. These wines offer incredible value within Burgundy & pair best with a juicy veggie burger topped with mushrooms and cheese.","path":"/product/domaine-gaget-cote-du-py-morgon-2023/4056257"},{"id":"2137589","sku":"ELY2137589_2022","name":"Domaine de l'Amandine Cotes du Rhone Villages Seguret 2022","vintage":2022,"varietal":"Rhone Blends","origin":"Cotes du Rhone Villages, Rhone, France","country":"France","region":"Cotes du Rhone Villages","myRating":4.5,"ratedDate":"7/15/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":3.7,"communityCount":34,"critics":[{"score":94,"source":"WineEnthusiast"},{"score":92,"source":"WilfredWong"}],"priceUsd":null,"attrs":[],"sommName":null,"sommWriteup":null,"path":"/product/domaine-de-lamandine-cotes-du-rhone-villages-seguret-2022/2137589"},{"id":"2562412","sku":"PIN605053_2022","name":"Shatter Grenache 2022","vintage":2022,"varietal":"Grenache","origin":"Maury, Roussillon, South of France, France","country":"France","region":"Maury","myRating":2.5,"ratedDate":"7/9/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":3.6,"communityCount":30,"critics":[{"score":93,"source":"JamesSuckling"}],"priceUsd":21.97,"attrs":[],"sommName":"Josefina","sommWriteup":"As a fan of Grenache, you'll love this French collaboration between famed U.S. winemaker Joel Gott and legendary Rhone ranger, Charles Bieler. This is a lush Southern French expression of black fruits and cocoa notes. Decant!","path":"/product/shatter-grenache-2022/2562412"},{"id":"2669489","sku":"TON99167_22_2022","name":"BenMarco Malbec 2022","vintage":2022,"varietal":"Malbec","origin":"Uco Valley, Mendoza, Argentina","country":"Argentina","region":"Uco Valley","myRating":null,"ratedDate":null,"pickedForYou":"7/2/26","communityAvg":4.1,"communityCount":125,"critics":[{"score":93,"source":"JamesSuckling"},{"score":91,"source":"Vinous"},{"score":90,"source":"WineSpectator"}],"priceUsd":null,"attrs":[],"sommName":"Josefina","sommWriteup":"This is a personal favorite from Argentina's Uco Valley in Mendoza that checks all the boxes in terms of flavor. Structured and succulent, pair it with grilled veggies and hearty stews. Worth decanting it for 20-30 minutes.","path":"/product/benmarco-malbec-2022/2669489"},{"id":"4124320","sku":"WBO30338691_2023","name":"Morgante Nero d'Avola 2023","vintage":2023,"varietal":"Nero d'Avola","origin":"Sicily, Italy","country":"Italy","region":"Sicily","myRating":4.5,"ratedDate":"6/9/26","pickedForYou":null,"communityAvg":3.8,"communityCount":5,"critics":[],"priceUsd":23.97,"attrs":[],"sommName":"Aimee","sommWriteup":"A native Sicilian varietal known for its bold darkberry and plum fruit. Robust tannins and a touch of bright acidity make it a great wine to match with meat based sauces and stews or veggie options like rich lentil soups or grilled portobellos.","path":"/product/morgante-nero-davola-2023/4124320"},{"id":"3300350","sku":"MSE561768_2024","name":"Domaine Bousquet Reserve Organic Pinot Noir 2024","vintage":2024,"varietal":"Pinot Noir","origin":"Uco Valley, Mendoza, Argentina","country":"Argentina","region":"Uco Valley","myRating":null,"ratedDate":null,"pickedForYou":"6/2/26","communityAvg":3.8,"communityCount":5,"critics":[{"score":91,"source":"JamesSuckling"}],"priceUsd":18.97,"attrs":["Green"],"sommName":null,"sommWriteup":null,"path":"/product/domaine-bousquet-re